title:
Auto-disarm in RTL reported

body:
There seems to be a scary bug where RTL caused all motors to stop immediately in flight.

More details in https://groups.google.com/forum/#!topic/px4users/UxPZQ6G4KVs.

comments:
[issue_comment] julianoes | created=2016-07-16T15:33:18Z | updated=2016-07-16T15:33:18Z | https://github.com/PX4/PX4-Autopilot/issues/5083#issuecomment-233135826
I had a look at the 4 logfiles:

16_27_18.px4log -> crash out of air
15_55_33.px4log -> "crash" handheld
16_41_48.px4log -> "crash" handheld
16_39_57.px4log -> all correct, handheld

I believe there are two things happening in combination which leads to the unexpected behaviour:
1. The land detector publishes "landed" which is wrong.
2. The auto disarm timeout doesn't work because the land detector only publishes when it changes meaning the check below doesn't work as expected:

```
/* Update land detector */
orb_check(land_detector_sub, &updated);
if (updated) {
    orb_copy(ORB_ID(vehicle_land_detected), land_detector_sub, &land_detector);

    if (disarm_when_landed > 0) {
        if (land_detector.landed) {
            if (_inair_last_time > 0 &&
                (hrt_elapsed_time(&_inair_last_time) > (hrt_abstime)disarm_when_landed * 1000 * 1000)) {
                arm_disarm(false, &mavlink_log_pub, "auto disarm on land");
                _inair_last_time = 0;
            }
        } else {
            _inair_last_time = land_detector.timestamp;
        }
    }

    was_landed = land_detector.landed;
    was_falling = land_detector.freefall;
}
```

It looks like `_inair_last_time` gets only updated every time the state changes and is therefore set to the time at takeoff, so clearly more than the timeout in the past. Thus the auto_disarm would trigger immediately.


---

[issue_comment] julianoes | created=2016-07-16T17:16:37Z | updated=2016-07-16T17:16:37Z | https://github.com/PX4/PX4-Autopilot/issues/5083#issuecomment-233140793
I tried to find a cause why the land detector would detect a landing (1.):

In POSCTL `flag_control_manual_enabled` is `true` which means the land detector [decides to in-air solely on manual input z](https://github.com/PX4/Firmware/blob/master/src/modules/land_detector/MulticopterLandDetector.cpp#L194), so throttle. 
This means the histeresis timer called `_landTimer` is not updated.

Once, we switch from POSCTL to RTL `flag_control_manual_enabled` is `false`, meaning we look at these 4 bools:

```
    if (verticalMovement || rotating || !minimalThrust || horizontalMovement) {
        // Sensed movement or thottle high, so reset the land detector.
        _landTimer = now;
        return false;
    }
```

In calm hover, all flags will be `false` except `!minimalThrust`. Unfortunately, in the crash log (16_27_18.px4log), there is one small blip where thrust is 0 right at the moment of the switch from POSCTL to RTL.

I tried to reproduce this in SITL by injecting `actuators.control[3] = 0.0f;` right at the moment of a mode switch and was able to reproduce the copter falling out of the air.

**I'm not totally convinced yet that I've found "the" case, I might be on a wrong track. However, the issues found need fixing anyway.**


---

